&lt;h2&gt;Job Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Digital Marketing Associate to support execution across every surface where Doma and D3 show up: social, digital events, content, campaigns, and reporting. This is a generalist role on a small, fast-moving team. In one week you might edit a YouTube clip, run production for an X Space, pull campaign numbers into a weekly report, write a thread, and build a Luma page. This is a first or second job in marketing, and it moves at startup speed. If you want a repeatable checklist, this is not the role. If you want reps across the full marketing stack at an early-stage crypto infrastructure company, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Social Marketing&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support daily publishing across X, LinkedIn, and YouTube: drafting, scheduling, formatting, and posting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own community listening and engagement queues, surfacing replies and mentions worth a response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test and build new channels (TikTok, Farcaster, Telegram, short-form video) and report back on what works&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the content calendar and keep contributors on deadline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce social graphics, event flyers, and slide edits from existing brand templates in Figma or Canva, Manage the asset library and keep versions organized&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brief and coordinate with our visual designer and outside contractors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build weekly and monthly performance reports across social, web, email, and campaign channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track UTMs, tag links, and keep attribution clean&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep track of reporting. Turn numbers into a point of view. Tell us what to do more of and what to kill&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Digital Events&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run production for X Spaces, webinars, AMAs, and podcast recordings: run-of-show, speaker prep, reminders, recording, and follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build event pages, registration flows, and reminder sequences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cut recordings into clips, quote cards, and recap posts within 48 hours of the event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Content Creation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft social copy, newsletter sections, event recaps, and blog support material&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Repurpose long-form assets (reports, podcasts, panels) into channel-native formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep our voice consistent for two audiences at once: domain industry veterans and crypto-native traders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Launch Campaign Support&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support go-to-market for protocol upgrades, partner announcements, and token launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain campaign trackers, asset checklists, and launch-day run-of-show&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate KOL toolkits, partner co-marketing assets, and community distribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-to-3 years of relevant marketing experience. Agency, startup, or in-house all count&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management instincts: you track your own deadlines, you chase down blockers, and nothing falls through the cracks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with incomplete information. You make a call, flag the assumption, and keep moving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sense of ownership. You treat a task as yours from brief to published, including the unglamorous parts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to context-switch across five projects in a day without losing the thread&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, fast writing. Short sentences, no AI slop filler&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working fluency with the modern marketing stack: social schedulers, analytics dashboards, Figma or Canva, Notion or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working async across time zones with a distributed team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web3 or crypto background. Ideal, not required. Curiosity and a fast learning curve matter more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain industry exposure, or a genuine interest in how the internet&#39;s naming layer works&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Video editing chops and a feel for short-form pacing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running live audio or webinar production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic HTML, CSS, or no-code site building (Claude Code, Webflow, Framer)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data comfort: spreadsheets, dashboards, light SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meme literacy. You know the difference between funny and cringe, and you know which accounts set the tone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
