&lt;li&gt;Fix bugs, improve performance, and optimize existing features with guidance from senior engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and apply best practices in accessibility, SEO, and responsive design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay curious about new technologies and contribute ideas to improve user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related field (or equivalent practical experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0–2 years of experience in frontend development (internships, projects, or open-source work all count).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern JavaScript frameworks (React preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of HTML, CSS, and responsive design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Git version control and collaborative coding practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in blockchain/Web3 technologies is a plus, but not required—you’ll learn on the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, eagerness to learn, and ability to work in a team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CSS frameworks (e.g., Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Web3 libraries like ethers.js or web3.js.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with mobile-first design and accessibility principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous coursework, projects, or internships involving blockchain, NFTs, or dApps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
